{"v":"3.0.0","project":{"accession":"PRJNA1497305","title":"Sludge from different conductive material mediated groups Genome sequencing and assembly","description":"Microbial communities evolved from weak spatial differentiation during startup toward niche specific organization under high loading. Hydrolytic and acidogenic bacteria were preferentially enriched in bottom sludge, whereas syntrophic bacteria and Methanothrix became increasingly abundant in suspended sludge. In parallel, carrier biofilms evolved from initial colonization sites into functional interfaces that coupled intermediate conversion with methanogenesis and connected the bottom and suspended sludge. Under extreme organic loading, bacterial and archaeal communities in both sludge niches converged toward simplified assemblages dominated by Clostridium and Methanobacterium, respectively, and the biofilm in R1 underwent a similar simplification. By contrast, the biofilm in R2 retained multiple methanogens, including Methanothrix, Methanobacterium, and Methanolinea, thereby preserving spatial metabolic continuity under shock.","organism":"sludge metagenome","data_type":"Genome sequencing and assembly","center_name":"Xi'an University of Architecture and Technology","submission_date":"2026/07/18 00:00","last_update":null},"sample_cols":["accession","title","collection_date","country","region","city","lat","lon","urban_status","urban_context","eligibility_reason","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","host","location_resolution","country_iso2","place_id","location_status","location_method","location_note","geo_loc_raw","collection_year"],"samples":[["SAMN61798244","MIMARKS Survey related sample from metagenome","2025-08-16T13:45:30Z","China","Shaanxi","Xi’an",34.24,108.97,"probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","city-level location without sample-site confirmation",null,"engineered","anaerobic digester sludge",null,null,"coordinate","CN",1790630,"verified","text+coordinates",